meta {
  name: Search Products - Pagination
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products?_fields=id&_fields=sku&_page=1&_page_size=2
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data: isArray
  res.body.pagination.next_page: contains _page=2
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against "David's Dev Account".

  ## What it does
  `GET /api/v3/products` with `_page`/`_page_size` -- one of the two
  "Possible Alternative" pagination styles listed in `API V3.md` (~line
  191). Confirmed working: returns exactly 2 results and a `next_page`
  link that itself carries `_page=2&_page_size=2` forward.

  ## Pagination dialect findings (Phase 0)
  - **Default/no params**: page size defaults to **25**; `pagination`
    always carries a `next_page` full-URL link (cursor/link-style), e.g.
    `.../products?_fields=id&_page=2`. This is the primary, always-present
    pagination mechanism.
  - **`_page`+`_page_size`**: confirmed working (this request).
  - **`_offset`+`_limit`**: confirmed **NOT working** --
    `400 {"errors":[{"name":"InvalidFieldError","description":"Field
    '_offset' does not exist in model 'Product'."}]}`. The offset/limit
    "Possible Alternative" style in `API V3.md` is not implemented for
    this resource/version.
  - **`_sort_by=<field>`**: confirmed working, e.g. `_sort_by=sku` returns
    results in ascending SKU order.

  Given `openapi_pimv3.json` declares none of these params (see
  `List Products.bru`'s docs), all of the above had to be discovered
  empirically -- see `config/api-testing.config.md` quirks #8-9.
}
